# Post-Change Verification

After making any code changes, run these checks before finishing the task:

```bash
npm run lint
npx tsc --noEmit
```

## Requirements

- Run both commands after edits to source files, config, or tests.
- If either command fails, fix the reported issues before considering the task complete.
- Re-run the failing command after each fix until both pass.
- Skip only when the task was read-only (no files were modified).

## Automated Hook

Project hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` also enforce this workflow:

- `afterFileEdit` marks when source files are edited.
- `stop` runs `npm run lint` and `npx tsc --noEmit` when edits were made.
- If checks fail, the agent receives a follow-up message to fix the issues (up to 5 loops).

## Notes

- `npm run lint` runs ESLint with zero warnings allowed (`eslint . --max-warnings=0`).
- `npx tsc --noEmit` performs a full-project TypeScript check without emitting files.
- These match the pre-commit hook checks in `.husky/pre-commit`.
